# Thread 1 — ⚠️ IMPORTANT: the structured+classic mixed shape never joins the classic-folded paths into the working set

Fixed — the structured branch of `_projectMessages` now forwards `dropped: classicHidden`, exactly the one-liner the pure-classic branch at `session_tree.dart:721` already used.

**Commit**: `ccea68d128` — `gh-210 rework: review thread 1 (IMPORTANT) — join classic-folded writes into the working set in the structured+classic mixed shape`

```dart
    return _withLevel0Blocks(
      renderStructuredMessages(
        path: path,
        seqs: seqs,
        projectEntry: (record) =>
            _entryToMessages(record, classicHidden: classicHidden, seqs: seqs),
      ),
      path: path,
      entries: entries,
      // The mixed shape: classic-folded records join the working set scan
      // here too — the pure-classic branch forwards the same drop.
      dropped: classicHidden,
    );
```

(`lib/src/session/session_tree.dart`, structured branch of `_projectMessages`.)

**Test** (RED first — it failed on the pre-fix tree with the working-set block absent entirely, because the kept path had no write calls left): `test/compaction/working_set_projection_test.dart` → *"MIXED shape: classic-folded writes re-inject under structured hides too (the structured branch forwards the classic drop)"*. It builds the exact reachable shape from the finding: a structured `HiddenRangeRecord` that survives the classic cut (sits after `firstKeptEntryId`, so the projection takes the structured branch), a classic `CompactionRecord` coexisting on the path (the structured→classic fall-through shape), and the `write lib/auth.dart` pair inside the folded region — then asserts the path renders in the files section (`- lib/auth.dart`), the counting heading is present, and `validateToolPairing` stays empty. The existing session-survival fixture (structured hide + classic compaction + recitation) still passes unchanged, and the whole `test/compaction/ + test/session/` surface (960 tests) is green on the fixed tree.

# Thread 2 — 💡 SUGGESTION: flatten whitespace in rendered file paths — the goal line does, paths don't

Fixed — the one-line-per-fact rule now covers file paths too, mirroring `_goalLine`.

**Commit**: `e2db4cf670` — `gh-210 rework: review thread 2 (SUGGESTION) — flatten whitespace in working-set file paths, one line per fact`

Applied at the derivation point rather than inside `assemble()` — `recentlyTouchedPaths` (`lib/src/compaction/working_set.dart`) is the only source of rendered paths, and normalizing there additionally keeps spelling dedup consistent (`'a\nb'` and `'a b'` collapse to one entry) and lets the char-budget loop measure the final strings:

```dart
      // One line per fact (the goal line's rule): a `\n` is legal in
      // POSIX filenames and model-emittable into tool arguments — verbatim
      // rendering would inject block structure (fake entries, fake
      // counting tails) into the system-tagged block. Whitespace
      // collapses here so the render and the budgets measure the final
      // strings, and spelling dedup stays consistent.
      final flattened = argument.replaceAll(RegExp(r'\s+'), ' ').trim();
      if (flattened.isEmpty) continue;
      lastMention[flattened] = i++;
```

**Test** (RED first — the pre-fix tree rendered the spoof verbatim, exactly as reported): `test/compaction/working_set_test.dart` → *"whitespace-carrying paths render as ONE flattened line"*. It uses the finding's own scenario: a `write` whose `path` argument is `'real.dart\n… and 9 more touched files'`, post-boundary. It asserts the flattened form `- real.dart … and 9 more touched files` renders, exactly one `- ` line exists, and the fake counting tail never appears at a line start (`isNot(contains('\n… and 9 more touched files'))`). Budget behavior is untouched (the budget loop still drops the oldest file until the block fits); the existing char-budget, max-paths, clip-marker and goal-flatten tests all pass unchanged.
